# NMEA 0183 sentences are terminated by CR LF, and the AIS fixtures are compared byte for byte
# against golden output. Line-ending normalisation would rewrite them on checkout on Windows
# and every round-trip test would fail on a difference no reader could see in a diff.
*.nmea -text

# The same rule for ADS-B frames, and for the same reason one step removed. These files are LF
# and the emitter produces LF, so a checkout that rewrote them to CRLF would fail
# test_the_ingest_round_trip_is_byte_exact on a difference no reader could see in a diff —
# `_parse_frames` tolerates CRLF on the way in, which is exactly what would make the failure
# look like an adapter defect rather than a checkout artefact.
*.adsb -text
